#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# key_complement

#% text
# `key_complement([a1, a2, ...])` gives the association of the entries of `a1` whose keys occur in none of `a2`, .... Each element may be an association, a list of rules or a single rule.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
key_complement([assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2), assoc(a -> 3, c -> 4)])
#% output
#= assoc(b -> 2)

#% cell
key_complement([[a -> 1, b -> 2], [a -> 2]])
#% output
#= assoc(b -> 2)

#% cell
key_complement([assoc(b -> 2)])
#% output
#= assoc(b -> 2)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `key_drop`, `keys`, `complement`
